<LegalPage title="Your inner life stays yours." lede="Indulge is a private, local-first iPhone app. This policy explains the current TestFlight build in plain language." path="/privacy/">
  <section><h2>What the app stores</h2><p>Indulge stores your onboarding choices, active trade, Focus entries, and history in the app’s local container on your device.</p></section>
  <section><h2>What we collect</h2><p>Indulge does not operate an account system, advertising SDK, cross-app tracking, or third-party analytics. The developer does not receive your profile, trades, notes, or history.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Apple services and TestFlight</h2><p>On supported devices, optional Apple Intelligence features can suggest bounded tags or reflections. The app’s core experience and manual choices remain available without them. When you install a beta through TestFlight, Apple may process beta diagnostics and feedback under Apple’s own terms and privacy policy.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Retention and deletion</h2><p>Your local data remains until you remove it in the app or delete the app. Deleting Indulge removes its local app data. Because there is no Indulge account or server-side profile, there is no remote copy for us to retrieve or delete.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Your choices</h2><p>You may leave optional onboarding questions unanswered. The current build does not request Screen Time authorization, and the core experience does not require network access.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Changes and contact</h2><p>If a future version adds active sync, accounts, or server processing, this policy and the App Store privacy disclosure will be updated before that version is distributed. Questions can be sent through the <a href="/support/">support page</a>.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Effective date</h2><p>Last updated 11 August 2026.</p></section>
</LegalPage>
